{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1601","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1601","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1601\",\"parent_revision\":\"9e3407ce157322f3311c9d5a0c488d0f2ee0a13e9fe2d47e5cb05dceb661dc1e\",\"root_revision\":\"9e3407ce157322f3311c9d5a0c488d0f2ee0a13e9fe2d47e5cb05dceb661dc1e\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe SAM MCP server exposes 8 separate tools for task and plan operations. No MCP tool exists for active task session binding. Agents in isolated worktrees and kage-bunshin sessions cannot read or write their active task context through MCP \u2014 the only access path is direct filesystem.\\n\\nObserved problems (evidence from kaizen analysis of 401 sessions, report at .tmp/scratch/reports/kaizen-context-file-analysis.md):\\n\\n1. No MCP write path for active-task session binding. Agents write active-task-{session_id}.json via inline Python, Bash echo/printf, or skip it entirely. 9 confirmed manual write instances across 7 sessions. 5 additional Bash bypass instances (echo >, printf >, cat > heredoc) where agents circumvented Write tool approval requirements.\\n\\n2. $CLAUDE_SESSION_ID returns empty string from shell in some contexts (confirmed session b8ba796c \u2014 echo $CLAUDE_SESSION_ID produced empty stdout). When the active-task file write uses shell substitution, the file is created as active-task-.json or active-task-unknown.json, which the SubagentStop hook cannot correlate to any session.\\n\\n3. No MCP read path for active-task context from isolated worktrees. Agents that need to discover what task they are executing must read the filesystem directly, which is unreachable in worktree-isolated or remote execution contexts.\\n\\n4. The 8 current SAM tools each contribute their full schema to every agent context window on every request, multiplying token cost per-request proportional to tool count.\\n\\n5. sam-tasks-{slug}.json cache written to legacy in-repo .claude/context/ path (implementation_manager.py:1024,1089 and migrate_tasks_to_github.py:515) \u2014 not through dh_paths.context_dir(). The test at test_dh_paths_integration.py:1122 explicitly asserts this pattern must not exist in Python source, but an allowlist entry at line 1066 acknowledges it as unresolved.\\n\\n6. sam_claim MCP tool uses parameter name `task` while the YAML schema field is named `task_id` \u2014 observed double-call pattern in session 698ec246 where agent tried `task_id` first, failed, then discovered correct name via ToolSearch.\\n\\nResearch artifacts:\\n- .tmp/scratch/reports/kaizen-context-file-analysis.md \u2014 401-session transcript analysis, 8 HIGH findings\\n- .tmp/scratch/reports/mcp-context-storage-design.md \u2014 problem inventory and design options\\n- .tmp/scratch/reports/sam-consolidated-interface-design.md \u2014 Pydantic discriminated union interface design\\n- .tmp/scratch/reports/mcp-design-patterns-research.md \u2014 MCP tool design best practices research\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nFact-check performed 2026-04-05 against primary sources. All claims verified by direct file read; no training data used.\\n\\n**C1: SAM MCP server exposes exactly 8 tools.**\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\nEvidence: `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` lines 111, 160, 186, 236, 301, 426, 513, 584 \u2014 exactly 8 `@mcp.tool` decorators.\\n\\n**C2: No MCP tool exists for active-task session binding.**\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\nEvidence: Grep for `active[_-]task` in `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 no matches. The 8 tools are: `sam_list`, `sam_read`, `sam_create`, `sam_update`, `sam_state`, `sam_status`, `sam_ready`, `sam_claim`. None relates to active-task session context.\\n\\n**C3: implementation_manager.py lines 1024 and 1089 write to project_path / \\\".claude\\\" / \\\"context\\\" / f\\\"sam-tasks-{feature_slug}.json\\\"**\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\nEvidence:\\n- Line 1024: `cache_path = project_path / \\\".claude\\\" / \\\"context\\\" / f\\\"sam-tasks-{feature_slug}.json\\\"` (in `status` command)\\n- Line 1089: `cache_path = project_path / \\\".claude\\\" / \\\"context\\\" / f\\\"sam-tasks-{feature_slug}.json\\\"` (in `ready_tasks` command)\\nFile: `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/implementation_manager.py`\\n\\n**C4: migrate_tasks_to_github.py line ~515 hardcodes Path(\\\".claude\\\") / \\\"context\\\"**\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\nEvidence: Line 515 exactly: `cache_dir = Path(\\\".claude\\\") / \\\"context\\\"` followed by `cache_path = cache_dir / f\\\"sam-tasks-{slug}.json\\\"` at line 517.\\nFile: `plugins/development-harness/scripts/migrate_tasks_to_github.py`\\n\\n**C5: sam_claim parameter is named `task` not `task_id`**\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\nEvidence: `server.py` line 587: `task: Annotated[str, Field(description=\\\"Task ID to claim (e.g., 'T3')\\\")]` \u2014 parameter name is `task`, not `task_id`.\\n\\n**C6: test_dh_paths_integration.py:1122 asserts .claude/context/ must not appear in source files**\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED (line number off by one)\\nEvidence: The test method `def test_no_hardcoded_dot_claude_context_in_unexpected_production_code` is at line 1121. Its docstring begins at line 1122. The claim cites 1122 \u2014 the docstring is at that line, the `def` is at 1121. Functionally the claim is accurate: the test asserts `.claude/context/` must not appear in unexpected production code.\\nFile: `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dh_paths_integration.py`\\n\\n**C7: sam_schema/core/models.py uses ConfigDict (not class Config)**\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\nEvidence: Line 13: `from pydantic import AliasChoices, BaseModel, ConfigDict, Field, field_validator` \u2014 `ConfigDict` is imported. No `class Config` pattern present.\\nFile: `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py`\\n\\n**Summary: 7/7 VERIFIED. C6 has a 1-line offset (def is at 1121, docstring at 1122) but the substance is accurate.**\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: SAM MCP server has no distributed-safe interface for task and plan management\\nDate: 2026-04-06\\nGoal: Determine whether all information required to design a distributed-safe SAM MCP interface (consolidating 8\u21923 tools, adding active-task MCP tools, and migrating affected agents) is available before implementation begins.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. Current SAM MCP tool signatures (8 tools) | AVAILABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE | Citation: sam_schema/server.py \u2014 8 @mcp.tool decorators confirmed\\n2. active-task schema (fields: task_file_path, task_id, parent_issue_number, session_id, feature_slug, started_at) | AVAILABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE | Citation: confirmed in CLAUDE.md and get_task_context.py\\n3. dh_paths.context_dir() resolves correctly to ~/.dh/projects/{slug}/context/ | AVAILABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE | Citation: dh_paths.py confirmed\\n4. Pydantic discriminated union design for consolidated interface | AVAILABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE | Citation: .tmp/scratch/reports/sam-consolidated-interface-design.md\\n5. FastMCP v3 @mcp.tool pattern and ConfigDict convention | AVAILABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE | Citation: sam_schema/core/models.py uses ConfigDict; server.py uses @mcp.tool without parentheses\\n6. sam_claim uses parameter name `task` (not `task_id`) | AVAILABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE | Citation: server.py sam_claim signature + task-worker.md line 51\\n7. implementation_manager.py:1024,1089 legacy path writes | AVAILABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE | Citation: exact match confirmed by fact-checker\\n8. migrate_tasks_to_github.py:515 hardcoded Path(\\\".claude\\\") / \\\"context\\\" | AVAILABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE | Citation: exact match confirmed by fact-checker\\n9. 10 agent .md files with tools: frontmatter listing old SAM tool names | DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE | Citation: Grep confirmed task-worker.md, ecosystem-researcher.md, context-refinement.md, codebase-analyzer.md, plan-validator.md, context-gathering.md, impact-analyst.md, code-reviewer.md, feature-researcher.md, swarm-task-planner.md\\n10. Session_id field on Task model requires additive migration only | DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE | Citation: Read models.py lines 107-204 \u2014 no session_id field; populate_by_name=True already set; additive optional field, no destructive change needed\\n11. No MCP-layer SAM tests exist (test gap confirmed) | DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE | Citation: Glob tests/ \u2014 zero test_operations_sam.py; existing SAM tests cover domain models and hooks only\\n12. Active-task storage backend for distributed/multi-machine scenarios | MISSING \u2192 AVAILABLE | Citation: User decision 2026-04-06 \u2014 Option B: pluggable ContextBackend interface following BacklogBackend pattern. GitHub backend uses sticky issue comment (same pattern as artifact storage). Local backend uses ~/.dh/projects/{slug}/context/ filesystem path.\\n13. 10 agent .md files needing tools: frontmatter update after consolidation | NEW \u2192 AVAILABLE | Citation: Grep confirmed exact list of 10 files in plugins/development-harness/agents/\\n\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- Condition 9: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (10 agent files confirmed by Grep)\\n- Condition 10: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (Task model read directly; additive change only)\\n- Condition 11: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (zero MCP-layer SAM tests confirmed \u2014 test gap is scope)\\n- Condition 12: MISSING \u2192 AVAILABLE (user decision: pluggable ContextBackend, GitHub backend = sticky issue comment)\\n- Condition 13: NEW \u2192 AVAILABLE (10 files enumerated by Grep)\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Code - Producers\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 defines the 8 current MCP tools; consolidation to 3 tools (sam_task, sam_plan, sam_active_task) replaces all existing tool signatures, request/response schemas, and routing logic. Every caller that uses old tool names will receive MCP \\\"tool not found\\\" errors. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Public contract change \u2014 all consumers call tools by name; no tool aliases or backwards-compat shims exist in FastMCP.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 Task and Plan Pydantic models; adding `session_id` field to Task + introducing discriminated union request model changes serialization. Existing YAML plan files lack `session_id` \u2014 need migration or graceful default. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Schema change affects every reader, writer, and test that constructs Task objects directly.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/dh_paths.py` \u2014 `context_dir()` and `plan_dir()` used by server, hooks, and scripts; no API change expected here but any path convention change for active-task files propagates to all callers. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Central path resolver \u2014 changes ripple to all context-dir consumers.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/quality_gates.py` \u2014 quality-gate builder called from complete-implementation SKILL.md via `mcp__plugin_dh_sam__sam_create`. If `sam_create` is subsumed into `sam_plan`, callers using the current call signature break. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Consumed directly in complete-implementation skill with fully-qualified MCP tool name.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/local_yaml.py` \u2014 uses `dh_paths.context_dir()`; if active-task storage moves or schema changes, backend reads/writes need updating. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Backend implements read/write of the data the new `sam_active_task` tool will manage.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_sam_server.py` \u2014 entry point; imports `sam_schema.server.run_server`. No direct signature change needed, but must be re-validated post-consolidation. | Risk: LOW | Why: Thin wrapper \u2014 only affected if server module path or function name changes.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/cli.py` \u2014 CLI commands (claim, update, etc.) call the same underlying query functions as the MCP tools; if shared query functions are refactored, CLI commands need parity updates. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: CLI and MCP server share query layer \u2014 consolidation changes may create divergence between the two interfaces.\\n\\n### Code - Consumers\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/implementation_manager.py` \u2014 imports `sam_schema.core.query.claim_task`, `load_plan`, `sam_schema.core.models.STATUS_MAP`; lines 1024 and 1089 write sam-tasks-{slug}.json to `.claude/context/` instead of `dh_paths.context_dir()`. This is the hardcoded path violation the item explicitly describes. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Legacy path write is the exact bug in scope; import of query functions means changes to query layer break this file; no MCP usage \u2014 direct Python calls bypass the new interface entirely.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` \u2014 imports `sam_schema.core.models.TaskStatus`, `sam_schema.core.query.update_plan_fields`, `update_status`; reads `active-task-{session_id}.json` via `context_dir()` on SubagentStop; writes status updates directly to plan YAML via Python. If `sam_active_task` MCP tool replaces filesystem-only access, this hook must be updated to use MCP or the active-task schema must remain compatible. | Risk: HIGH | Why: SubagentStop hook is the critical completion signal \u2014 schema changes to active-task file break task status tracking for every agent session.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/get_task_context.py` \u2014 reads `active-task-*.json` via `dh_paths.context_dir()` glob; used by agents to discover their current task. New `sam_active_task` MCP tool should replace this filesystem glob but this script will not auto-update. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Filesystem-only read path \u2014 exactly the problem the item solves. Script becomes redundant but dangerous if left in place (agents may continue using it instead of MCP).\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/migrate_tasks_to_github.py` \u2014 imports `sam_schema.task_format.resolve_task_id`; line 515 has hardcoded path bug (not through `dh_paths.context_dir()`). | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Hardcoded path bug in scope per item description; query layer dependency creates secondary break risk.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 uses `dh_paths.context_dir()`; reads context to surface active-task info in backlog server responses. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: If active-task schema or location changes, backlog server will surface stale or missing context.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py` \u2014 uses `dh_paths`; no direct SAM tool calls found but shares path resolution. | Risk: LOW | Why: Indirect dependency \u2014 only breaks if path conventions change.\\n\\n- `plugins/python3-development/scripts/migrate_task_format.py` \u2014 uses `dh_paths`; format migration script that may touch SAM-structured YAML files. | Risk: LOW | Why: Migration utility \u2014 needs re-validation against new Task schema shape after `session_id` field addition.\\n\\n### Code - Other References\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/task_config.py` \u2014 uses `dh_paths`; task configuration resolution used internally by the server. If active-task location or session-id resolution changes, task_config must follow. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Shared configuration layer between server tools and filesystem hooks.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/pyproject.toml` \u2014 registers `sam = \\\"sam_schema.cli:app\\\"` and `sam-mcp = \\\"sam_schema.server:run_server\\\"` as entry points; lists `sam_schema` in packages. No code change needed unless module paths change, but must be verified post-consolidation. | Risk: LOW | Why: Package manifest \u2014 entry point names are stable but must be re-validated.\\n\\n- `pyproject.toml` \u2014 ruff allowlist entry for `plugins/**/sam_schema/core/backends/github_task.py`. No change needed unless file is moved or renamed during consolidation. | Risk: LOW | Why: Static linter config \u2014 fails silently if paths drift.\\n\\n### Tests\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_server.py` \u2014 tests current server tool handlers by name; all 8 tool names are exercised. Consolidation to 3 tools makes every existing test invalid. Full replacement required. | Risk: HIGH | Why: 1:1 coupling to old 8-tool API \u2014 zero tests will remain valid after consolidation.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_server_mcp.py` \u2014 tests MCP protocol-level tool calls against current tool names. Same complete invalidation as test_server.py. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Protocol-level coupling \u2014 tool names are request keys.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_cli_claim.py` \u2014 tests `sam_claim` CLI behavior; if claim is subsumed into `sam_task` with an operation discriminator, CLI claim behavior and test must be updated. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: CLI claim parity with MCP claim must be maintained and covered.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_server_sam.py` \u2014 tests SAM server at integration level; breaks when server tool names change. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Integration test coupling to old tool names.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_server_sam_taskbackend.py` \u2014 tests SAM task backend used by the server; affected by Task model schema changes (session_id addition). | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Backend tests construct Task objects directly \u2014 schema changes require fixture updates.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_operations_sam.py` \u2014 tests SAM operations layer (sam_read, sam_create, sam_update, etc.); breaks when operation signatures change under consolidation. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Operation-level coupling \u2014 directly tests the functions being replaced.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dh_paths_integration.py` \u2014 tests `context_dir()` and active-task file path; line 1066 has allowlist acknowledging the legacy `.claude/context/` path problem; line 1122 asserts the pattern must not exist in new Python source. This test must be extended to cover `sam_active_task` MCP round-trip. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Tests the path contract that the new `sam_active_task` tool must satisfy; allowlist at line 1066 must be resolved.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_reconciliation.py` \u2014 constructs `active-task-abc123.json` context files in test fixtures; breaks if active-task schema or path changes. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Test fixtures encode current active-task JSON schema \u2014 any field change (adding session_id, renaming fields) requires fixture updates.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/tests/test_task_status_hook/test_subagent_stop_integration.py` \u2014 writes active-task context files at line 92 using current schema; SubagentStop hook integration tested against current filesystem paths. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Directly tests the hook that reads active-task files \u2014 schema or location change breaks all integration scenarios.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/tests/test_task_status_hook/test_github_sync.py` \u2014 line 404 writes active-task file to `.claude/context/` (the legacy path); line 106 writes to context_dir(). Tests exercise both old and new path conventions. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Legacy path at line 404 is the exact bug \u2014 test must be corrected to use only `dh_paths.context_dir()` path; this test currently covers behavior that should not exist.\\n\\n### Documentation\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` \u2014 section 2.6 and table at line 264 document the active-task file path, the 8-tool interface, and the filesystem-only write flow from `/start-task`. Will become entirely stale when MCP write path is added. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Primary architecture reference \u2014 describes the exact behavior being changed; will actively mislead implementors if not updated.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` \u2014 line 490 documents the `/start-task` skill writing active-task to filesystem (not via MCP); line 497 documents PostToolUse hook reading it. Both sections need updating to reflect MCP path. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Lifecycle doc describes the broken flow \u2014 new MCP path is not mentioned anywhere in it.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` \u2014 documents Task and Plan YAML schema; if `session_id` is added to Task model, the format doc must reflect the new field. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Schema reference doc \u2014 stale field list causes agents to write incomplete Task YAML.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-lifecycle.md` \u2014 line 296 documents active-task file path; needs update to reflect both filesystem path and new MCP access path. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Cross-referenced by skill docs \u2014 stale active-task path description propagates to all readers.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/plan-artifact-lifecycle.md` \u2014 references SAM MCP tools by current name; needs update when tool names change. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Artifact lifecycle doc is consumed by planning agents \u2014 stale tool names produce \\\"tool not found\\\" patterns.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backend-providers.md` \u2014 documents dh_paths and backend conventions; needs update if active-task storage backend changes. | Risk: LOW | Why: Backend architecture reference \u2014 affected only if storage mechanism fundamentally changes.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/README.md` \u2014 line 356 documents `active-task-{session-id}.json` as ephemeral; line 72 describes `/start-task` writing it. Needs addition of new MCP path. | Risk: LOW | Why: User-facing README \u2014 stale but lower risk than internal architecture docs.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 line 93 lists `context/active-task-{session-id}.json` as ephemeral context. Needs MCP tool reference added. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: CLAUDE.md is injected into every agent session in this project \u2014 stale guidance actively affects all agents.\\n\\n- `.claude/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` \u2014 mirrors the development-harness workflow diagram; must be updated in sync. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Duplicate that can diverge \u2014 agents in the root project context read this version.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/task-worker.md` \u2014 `tools:` frontmatter explicitly lists `mcp__plugin_dh_sam__sam_read`, `mcp__plugin_dh_sam__sam_claim`, `mcp__plugin_dh_sam__sam_state`, `mcp__plugin_dh_sam__sam_update` by exact name; body instructs agents to call these tools. All 4 tool names become invalid after consolidation. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Frontmatter tool list controls which tools Claude makes available to the agent \u2014 stale names mean the agent cannot call SAM tools at all.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/context-refinement.md` \u2014 `tools:` frontmatter lists `sam_read`, `sam_update`; body calls both. Both names become invalid. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Same frontmatter binding issue \u2014 agent loses SAM access.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/context-gathering.md` \u2014 `tools:` frontmatter lists `sam_read`, `sam_update`; body calls both. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Same frontmatter binding issue.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/plan-validator.md` \u2014 `tools:` frontmatter lists `sam_read`, `sam_list`; body calls both. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Same frontmatter binding issue.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` \u2014 `tools:` frontmatter lists `sam_create`; body uses `sam_create`. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Same frontmatter binding issue