- `pyproject.toml` | Role: configuration | Connection: ruff allowlist path for sam_schema backend file | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n\\n### Risk Summary\\n\\n- Overall system risk: HIGH\\n- Highest-risk systems:\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 public contract change; all 8 tool names disappear, replaced by 3 new names; no consumer auto-migrates\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` \u2014 SubagentStop hook reads active-task files; schema or path change breaks task status tracking for every agent session in the repo\\n  - All 10 agent `.md` files with `tools:` frontmatter listing old SAM tool names \u2014 stale frontmatter means agents are silently denied access to SAM tools at session start with no error surfaced to the agent\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/skills/start-task/SKILL.md` \u2014 prescribes the broken shell-substitution pattern that produces `active-task-.json` (empty session ID) \u2014 this SKILL.md is the root cause delivery mechanism for bug #2 in the item description\\n- Main risk themes:\\n  - compatibility \u2014 8 tool names disappear; all consumers break at the MCP protocol level\\n  - agent-instruction \u2014 10 agent frontmatter files + 20 skill/reference files all encode old tool names; agents lose SAM tool access silently\\n  - verification \u2014 test suite for server tools (tests_sam/test_server.py, test_server_mcp.py, tests/test_server_sam.py, test_operations_sam.py) must be fully replaced; none of the existing tests survive consolidation\\n  - migration \u2014 active-task filesystem write in start-task SKILL.md must be replaced by MCP call; get_task_context.py filesystem glob must be superseded without being deleted prematurely (agents may still depend on it during transition)\\n  - behavioral \u2014 sam_claim parameter name mismatch (tool uses `task`, schema uses `task_id`) will recur in new interface unless fixed explicitly in new tool schema\\n- Scope expansion:\\n  - 10 agent `.md` files with stale frontmatter tool lists \u2014 not anticipated in item description (item focused on SKILL.md files and Python code)\\n  - `tests/test_github_sync.py` line 404 writes active-task to legacy `.claude/context/` path \u2014 this is an existing test that validates broken behavior; it must be corrected as part of this item, not separately\\n  - `.claude/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` (root project copy) \u2014 exists in addition to the development-harness copy; both must be updated\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every affected test updated or new coverage added\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated\\n- [ ] Every affected config or CI path updated and validated\\n- [ ] Every affected agent or skill instruction updated\\n- [ ] Replacement or migration coverage gaps resolved (active-task: filesystem write \u2192 MCP write; get_task_context.py glob \u2192 sam_active_task MCP read)\\n- [ ] Hidden transitive dependencies checked (sam_schema.core.query layer shared by CLI and MCP server; CLI parity must be maintained)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **sam mcp server has no distributed-safe interface for task and plan management** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 kaizen analysis of 401 sessions + design research 2026-04-06\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-06)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\nP1.\\n\\nEvidence base:\\n- 9 confirmed bypass sites write active-task state directly to `.claude/context/` via Bash or inline Python, circumventing any MCP-layer visibility or coordination control.\\n- 401 sessions affected per kaizen-context-file-analysis findings \u2014 the bypass is not hypothetical, it is the current execution path in production.\\n- Classification is `missing-guardrail`: no enforcement mechanism exists today. The PreToolUse[Bash] hook required by AC-10 cannot be added until the safe path (sam_active_task) exists \u2014 making this item the prerequisite for all active-task write safety.\\n- In distributed or parallel-agent runs, two agents writing `active-task-<session>.json` concurrently with no coordination produces silent corruption. The GitHub ContextBackend (AC-4) eliminates this race by making the sticky-comment write atomic at the GitHub API level.\\n- 10 agent files reference tool names that will cease to exist at the MCP protocol layer when the consolidated interface ships (AC-1, AC-2), causing silent tool loss for every agent that loads those files. The longer this ships without the frontmatter updates, the more agent runs silently lose SAM access.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nDirect consumers broken at MCP protocol level when old tools are removed:\\n- All agents with `tools:` frontmatter listing `sam_read`, `sam_claim`, `sam_state`, `sam_update`, `sam_create`, `sam_list`, `sam_ready`, `sam_status` \u2014 10 files confirmed in impact radius.\\n- `sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 8 tool registrations disappear; any MCP client enumerating tools gets a different tool list.\\n- `task_status_hook.py` (SubagentStop hook) \u2014 reads active-task files on task completion; a path or schema change without a coordinated sam_active_task migration breaks task completion signalling for every running agent.\\n- `implementation_manager.py` \u2014 two write sites that currently bypass MCP; after the hook (AC-10) ships, these become hard errors that halt plan execution.\\n- `start-task/SKILL.md` \u2014 currently prescribes the unsafe inline Python write; every agent loading this skill follows the blocked pattern after AC-10 ships.\\n- Secondary: any future plugin or agent that implements active-task writes by copying the current `implementation_manager.py` pattern will be blocked on first run.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n1. Single consolidated interface: callers use three tools (`sam_task`, `sam_plan`, `sam_active_task`) instead of eight, reducing the surface area agents must know.\\n2. Distributed-safe active-task storage: GitHub ContextBackend makes active-task state visible across sessions and agents without filesystem coordination; sticky issue comment is readable by any agent with access to the parent issue.\\n3. Enforceable guardrail: once `sam_active_task` is the only sanctioned write path, the PreToolUse[Bash] hook can block bypasses with a clear diagnostic \u2014 turning a silent corruption risk into a loud, actionable error.\\n4. MCP-layer test coverage: zero tests currently exist at this layer; AC-11 closes that gap and provides a regression baseline for all future SAM tool changes.\\n5. Agent file hygiene: 10 agent files receive correct tool names, restoring SAM access for all agents that load those files after the tool rename ships.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nAfter this item ships, an agent performing a SAM-managed task experiences the following:\\n\\n1. Agent calls `sam_task` with `action: claim` and a task ID \u2014 receives ownership confirmation. No equivalent `sam_claim` tool exists.\\n2. Agent calls `sam_active_task` with `action: set` and task context \u2014 active-task state is written to the ContextBackend (GitHub sticky comment in distributed mode, `dh_paths.context_dir()` file in local mode). No `.claude/context/` filesystem write occurs.\\n3. Agent calls `sam_task` with `action: state` to advance task status \u2014 state change recorded.\\n4. If agent attempts a Bash command that writes to `.claude/context/active-task*.json`, the PreToolUse[Bash] hook intercepts it and returns an error: `BLOCKED: direct active-task write intercepted. Use sam_active_task with action: set instead.`\\n5. On task completion, `task_status_hook.py` reads active-task state via `sam_active_task get` \u2014 not via direct filesystem path \u2014 and records completion correctly.\\n6. A second agent running in parallel against the same plan can read the same active-task state via `sam_active_task get` without filesystem access, because the GitHub ContextBackend stores it on the shared parent issue.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `sam_task` tool exists and accepts `action` discriminator values `read`, `claim`, `state`, `update` \u2014 the old tools `sam_read`, `sam_claim`, `sam_state`, `sam_update` are removed or emit a deprecation error redirecting callers to `sam_task`.\\n2. `sam_plan` tool exists and accepts `action` discriminator values `create`, `list`, `ready`, `status` \u2014 the old tools `sam_create`, `sam_list`, `sam_ready`, `sam_status` are removed or emit a deprecation error redirecting callers to `sam_plan`.\\n3. `sam_active_task` tool exists and accepts `action` discriminator values `get`, `set`, `update`, `clear` \u2014 each action performs the corresponding read/write operation against the configured ContextBackend without touching the filesystem directly.\\n4. GitHub ContextBackend: `sam_active_task set` writes active-task state as a sticky comment on the parent GitHub issue; `sam_active_task get` reads back that comment; `sam_active_task clear` removes it. No `.claude/context/` path is written.\\n5. Local ContextBackend: `sam_active_task` reads and writes to `dh_paths.context_dir()` \u2014 observable behaviour matches current behaviour for non-GitHub sessions.\\n6. `implementation_manager.py` lines 1024 and 1089 no longer contain direct filesystem writes to `.claude/context/`; both call `sam_active_task` (via MCP client or equivalent internal call) instead.\\n7. `migrate_tasks_to_github.py` line 515 references `dh_paths.context_dir()` \u2014 not a hardcoded `.claude/context/` path string.\\n8. All 10 agent `.md` files (`task-worker.md`, `ecosystem-researcher.md`, `context-refinement.md`, `codebase-analyzer.md`, `plan-validator.md`, `context-gathering.md`, `impact-analyst.md`, `code-reviewer.md`, `feature-researcher.md`, `swarm-task-planner.md`) have `tools:` frontmatter updated to list `sam_task`, `sam_plan`, `sam_active_task` \u2014 old tool names removed.\\n9. `start-task/SKILL.md` prescribes calling `sam_active_task` with `action: set` instead of the inline Python write or shell-substitution pattern that produces `active-task-.json`.\\n10. A `PreToolUse[Bash]` hook is present that detects and blocks shell commands writing to paths matching `.claude/context/active-task*.json`, emitting a clear error directing the caller to use `sam_active_task` instead.\\n11. MCP-layer tests exist covering: `sam_task` round-trip (read/claim/state/update), `sam_plan` round-trip (create/list/ready/status), and `sam_active_task` get/set/update/clear against both Local and GitHub ContextBackend. All tests pass in CI.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\nDesign artifacts produced during investigation:\\n- `.tmp/scratch/reports/sam-consolidated-interface-design.md` \u2014 Pydantic discriminated union design for `sam_task`, `sam_plan`, `sam_active_task`; action routing; backward-compatibility deprecation strategy\\n- `.tmp/scratch/reports/mcp-context-storage-design.md` \u2014 problem inventory, ContextBackend options analysis (local file, GitHub sticky comment, Redis), decision rationale\\n- `.tmp/scratch/reports/kaizen-context-file-analysis.md` \u2014 401-session evidence base; 8 HIGH findings including the 9 confirmed bypass sites and session_id collision risk\\n\\nRelated backlog context:\\n- P389 (BacklogBackend Protocol) \u2014 established the pluggable backend pattern this item extends to ContextBackend\\n\\n### Files\\n\\nCore implementation:\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 8 old tool registrations replaced with 3 consolidated tool registrations\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/implementation_manager.py` (lines 1024, 1089) \u2014 direct `.claude/context/` writes replaced with `sam_active_task` calls\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/migrate_tasks_to_github.py` (line 515) \u2014 hardcoded path replaced with `dh_paths.context_dir()`\\n\\nContextBackend:\\n- New file: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/context_backend.py` (or equivalent) \u2014 ContextBackend Protocol + Local and GitHub implementations\\n\\nHook:\\n- `.claude/hooks/` \u2014 new PreToolUse[Bash] hook blocking direct active-task writes\\n\\nAgent frontmatter (10 files, tools: field update):\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/task-worker.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/ecosystem-researcher.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/context-refinement.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/codebase-analyzer.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/plan-validator.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/context-gathering.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/impact-analyst.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/code-reviewer.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-researcher.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md`\\n\\nSkill:\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/start-task/SKILL.md` \u2014 inline Python write replaced with `sam_active_task` invocation\\n\\nTests:\\n- New file: `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_sam_mcp_tools.py` \u2014 MCP-layer tests for all three consolidated tools\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\nBlocked by:\\n- None identified. The ContextBackend Protocol pattern is established (P389). No schema migration of Task model is required \u2014 session_id is an additive optional field only.\\n\\nBlocks:\\n- PreToolUse[Bash] hook enforcement (AC-10) cannot ship safely until `sam_active_task` exists as the sanctioned alternative \u2014 that hook is part of this item's scope.\\n- Any future item adding distributed agent coordination features depends on GitHub ContextBackend being present.\\n- Agent file correctness for the 10 affected agents depends on the new tool names being registered before the old tools are removed.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nL (Large).\\n\\nRationale:\\n- Three new MCP tool definitions with Pydantic discriminated union schemas and full action routing (sam_task \u00d7 4 actions, sam_plan \u00d7 4 actions, sam_active_task \u00d7 4 actions).\\n- ContextBackend Protocol with two concrete implementations (Local, GitHub) \u2014 GitHub implementation requires sticky-comment read/write/delete against the GitHub Issues API.\\n- Two write-site refactors in implementation_manager.py requiring integration testing against both backends.\\n- Hook script for PreToolUse[Bash] with pattern matching and clear diagnostic output.\\n- 10 agent frontmatter edits \u2014 mechanical but must be verified individually (tools: field is load-time-parsed and silently drops unknown names).\\n- start-task/SKILL.md rewrite \u2014 skill content change requires behavioral test per repo convention.\\n- New MCP-layer test file covering 3 tools \u00d7 2 backends = minimum 6 integration test scenarios.\\n- Zero existing MCP-layer tests means no established test harness to extend \u2014 test infrastructure setup is part of the effort.\\n\\nNot XL because: no destructive schema migration, no multi-plugin coordination, and the ContextBackend pattern is directly analogous to the established BacklogBackend pattern.\\n\\n### Concerns\\n\\n- [x] server.py:1020 wildcard match arm makes remaining patterns unreachable \u2014 blocked sam_claim during T02. RESOLVED: Fixed in commit 849c4423 by T05/T06. Current server.py has exactly one `case _:` per tool function (L682, L773, L864). Verified 2026-04-06.\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Classification: missing-guardrail**\\n\\n**Rationale:** 9 instances across 7 sessions of agents writing `active-task-*.json` manually via inline Python/Bash are not the result of agent error or process drift \u2014 they are the only available code path. Every agent that calls `sam_claim` and then needs to register active-task context must bypass to direct filesystem access because `sam_set_active_task` does not exist. This is a structural enforcement gap, not a recurring agent mistake.\\n\\n**What the guardrail enforces:**\\nActive-task session context (which task an agent currently owns, its plan file, parent issue number) must be written exclusively through a SAM MCP tool (`sam_set_active_task`), never via Bash inline Python, `echo >`, `printf >`, or `cat > EOF` to `.claude/context/` or `~/.dh/` paths.\\n\\nThe guardrail has two components:\\n1. **Tool existence**: `sam_set_active_task` MCP tool must exist so agents have a compliant write path.\\n2. **Tool enforcement**: A `PreToolUse[Bash]` hook must detect `active-task` or `sam-tasks` patterns in commands targeting `.claude/context/` and block with a redirect message pointing to the MCP tool.\\n\\n**Evidence of gap (not agent error):**\\n- Session `0472fe57`: Agent tried `context_dir(session_id=session_id)` first (wrong API), then adapted \u2014 two-attempt exploration confirms the agent was navigating absent tooling, not ignoring available tooling.\\n- Session `a29195b1`: Explicit `|| echo \\\"Context write fallback\\\"` \u2014 agent acknowledged the write might fail and built anticipatory fallback. This is defensive coding against a tooling gap.\\n- Session `916a7807`: Orchestrator instructed agents to skip `sam_claim` when Bash was denied \u2014 the entire claim step was abandoned because no MCP-only path existed.\\n- Kaizen report: \\\"Root cause: No `sam_set_active_task` MCP tool exists. The only write path is direct filesystem access via embedded Python. This is a tooling gap, not an agent error.\\\" (Focus 1, Finding F1-A)\\n\\n**Recurrence mechanism:** The gap is structural. Until `sam_set_active_task` exists and the enforcement hook blocks the bypass, every session needing active-task registration will reproduce the pattern identically. Recurrence is determined by tool count, not by agent behavior variance.\\n\\n**Scope of enforcement gap:**\\n- Direct write bypasses: 9 instances / 7 sessions (confirmed inline Python or shell redirect)\\n- Legacy path writes from `implementation_manager.py`: systemic (20+ sessions, lines 1024 + 1089)\\n- Legacy path write from `migrate_tasks_to_github.py`: 1 file, line 515 (active bug)\\n- No blocking hook on `PreToolUse[Bash]`: confirmed absent (MH-1 in kaizen report)\\n\\n## Artifact Manifest\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:77a664ceae8cca392ef3fac0442f9b45 -->\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"388af8c9d79ec5c33a8f543d9be821036a27a5522abfcb1bb641979afca8585f\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVWAJdg\"}"}